        <h3>Roadside assistance</h3>
        <details><summary>What kind of roadside help can I get?</summary><div class="ans"><p>Battery and jump-start assistance, flat tyres, minor roadside mechanical problems, emergency fuel, vehicle breakdown assistance, and towing or recovery coordination where available.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How quickly will someone reach me?</summary><div class="ans"><p>We don't give arrival times. Your request goes out to available mechanics and roadside agents, and you're told once a provider has accepted. If we can't reach anyone, we'll tell you rather than leave you waiting.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>What should I do if I'm in danger?</summary><div class="ans"><p>Contact the appropriate emergency service first. That applies to any accident with injuries, fire, smoke, a medical emergency or another life-threatening situation. Get yourself and your passengers away from moving traffic before anything else.</p></div></details>
